                    "propertyValues": {
                        "html": {
                            "type": "TRANSLATION_LITERAL",
                            "value": {
                                "code": null,
                                "comment": "",
                                "message": "<p data-end=\"572\" data-start=\"267\">A Passkey is a secure and user-friendly method for verifying identity during login. Unlike traditional one-time passwords (OTPs), a passkey is stored securely on a user's device, such as a smartphone, laptop, or hardware security key and is used as a second factor in Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).</p>\n<p data-end=\"769\" data-start=\"574\">During login, the user simply approves the authentication request using biometrics (e.g., fingerprint, Face ID), a device PIN, or a hardware security key without needing to manually enter a code.</p>\n<p data-end=\"993\" data-start=\"771\">The ServiceNow platform supports FIDO2 Passkeys and Biometric Authentication methods such as Windows Hello, Apple Face ID, and Touch ID. Users must enroll once and can then authenticate using supported devices.</p>\n<h4 data-end=\"1009\" data-start=\"995\"><strong>Advantages</strong>:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"1009\" data-start=\"995\"><strong>Strongest security</strong>: Phishing-resistant and eliminates password-based vulnerabilities.</li>\n<li data-end=\"1009\" data-start=\"995\"><strong>Fast and seamless experience:</strong>&nbsp;Biometrics and device-native authentication provide a quick and smooth login process.</li>\n<li data-end=\"1009\" data-start=\"995\"><strong>No reliance on external OTP devices:</strong> Works across modern devices with built-in support</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-end=\"1595\" data-start=\"1483\">For a list of supported platforms and additional setup details, refer to the official <a href=\"/api/now/v1/context_doc_url/mfa-web-auth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">product documentation</a>.</p>"
                            }
                        }
                    },
